WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:06.658
Just quickly,
I'm Keyur Sorathia,

00:00:06.659 --> 00:00:08.760
I'm faculty member
at IIT Guwahati.

00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:11.736
I work in the area of HCI,
specifically in ICT4D, and

00:00:11.737 --> 00:00:14.522
we have just started working
in virtual reality and

00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:16.130
input interaction method.

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:19.020
So given the time frame we have,
ten minutes,

00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:21.880
I'll quickly brief you about
some of the projects that we

00:00:21.881 --> 00:00:23.600
are doing currently in Assam.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.590
And I'll be majorly talking
about two projects,

00:00:26.591 --> 00:00:29.470
which are very recent
project we have started.

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:33.574
The first one is Pragati, which
is basically trying to train

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.078
community health
workers in Assam.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:39.245
And the second one is Swasthyaa,
which is basically an ICT

00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:42.030
supported complete ecosystem for
Tuberculosis.

00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:44.996
Okay, these projects are funded
by government of India and

00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:47.904
they are collaborating with WHO,
Government of Assam and

00:00:47.905 --> 00:00:49.470
National Health Commission.

00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:52.265
I'll very briefly touch
upon what we are doing, and

00:00:52.266 --> 00:00:54.298
maybe if someone
has some questions,

00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:56.470
we can certainly talk
about them later.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.560
Okay, just a lot of people may
not sure that they are available

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:05.650
health workers but just to
give you a quick idea about,

00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:09.680
Health workers are sort of
people who communicate health

00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:13.280
education and act as a mediator
between the doctors and

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:14.290
the community members.

00:01:14.291 --> 00:01:17.906
So sometimes, they become
health professionals and

00:01:17.907 --> 00:01:21.614
support them in escorting to
health centers and so on.

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:24.514
So currently, what we see is
there are a lot of challenges,

00:01:24.515 --> 00:01:27.090
loopholes into the health
worker recruit system.

00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:30.246
So first is they're not
sufficiently trained.

00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:33.210
And even if they are trained,
the methods are very passive in

00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:36.071
nature, which includes
a variable method that someone,

00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:37.804
A trainer comes and
speaks about it and

00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:40.850
then expects all the health
workers to learn by themselves.

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:43.201
So what happens, and there
are other problems that I'm not

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.243
going to the detail of it.

00:01:44.244 --> 00:01:47.683
But because of this these
problems, the health workers

00:01:47.684 --> 00:01:51.195
are not able to gain health
education or training, which

00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.949
they are supposed to communicate
to the community members.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:58.764
And because of this, the healthy
communities, as in this results

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:02.330
basically in unhealthy practices
in the rural communities.

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:05.908
So what we have done is,
we have basically created,

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:10.130
designed the Low-cost Head
Mounted Display based immersive

00:02:10.131 --> 00:02:13.750
virtual interface that is
to train health workers.

00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:17.910
So, one of the good part of this
project, this is not a passive

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:22.231
set of modules, just audiovisual
modules where health workers

00:02:22.232 --> 00:02:25.527
would come and learn, or
listen to the modules.

00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:27.145
But, yet,
what we are trying to do,

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.864
it is giving them certain task
that they would be performing in

00:02:29.865 --> 00:02:31.140
various set of activities.

00:02:31.141 --> 00:02:32.890
So we can see over here.

00:02:32.891 --> 00:02:36.340
So you can see but the health
workers would actually take

00:02:36.341 --> 00:02:37.840
the baby out of the womb,

00:02:37.841 --> 00:02:40.280
perform those activities unto
the virtual environment.

00:02:40.281 --> 00:02:44.235
The second, where the health
worker would clean the new born,

00:02:44.236 --> 00:02:47.817
and health workers would make
the pregnant women sleep on

00:02:47.818 --> 00:02:49.246
the chair, and so on.

00:02:49.247 --> 00:02:52.070
So those kinds of activities
they will be performing.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:55.786
And the idea is that to have
hands on practice-based approach

00:02:55.787 --> 00:02:57.935
rather than just
a passive module.

00:02:57.936 --> 00:03:02.627
So the other interesting part of
this project is they wanted to

00:03:02.628 --> 00:03:04.720
scale the project test.

00:03:04.721 --> 00:03:07.820
The solution works with a Head
Mounted Display, as well as in

00:03:07.821 --> 00:03:11.160
a 2D mobile application, as well
as in a 360-degree environment.

00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:14.110
So we wanted to ensure that such
solutions are not limited to

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.061
training center,

00:03:15.062 --> 00:03:18.372
Which ideally would have
the cheap Head Mounted Displays,

00:03:18.373 --> 00:03:21.361
which the government of
Assam has agreed to provide.

00:03:21.362 --> 00:03:23.080
But it also goes
on to the field,

00:03:23.081 --> 00:03:25.885
where health worker can take
it onto the field, show

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:28.966
it to the community members,
And act as a third person,

00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:32.191
specifically in the issues
related to family planning,

00:03:32.192 --> 00:03:35.610
sex, and pregnancy,
which they are very shy about.

00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:38.030
So can mobile phone
become a third person

00:03:38.031 --> 00:03:40.170
where information
related to sex and so

00:03:40.171 --> 00:03:42.700
on could be communicated
to rural communities?

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.660
Through these mobile
interventions.

00:03:44.661 --> 00:03:47.484
And also, it works when
health worker is at home,

00:03:47.485 --> 00:03:50.751
they can also learn themselves,
sitting at their home.

00:03:50.752 --> 00:03:53.788
Okay, there are other part, I'm
not going to the videos right

00:03:53.789 --> 00:03:57.240
now, but the other part
of the solution is about

00:03:57.241 --> 00:04:00.210
a peer learning platform, Which
is the only audio and visual

00:04:00.211 --> 00:04:04.164
based peer learning platform,
where health workers, all across

00:04:04.165 --> 00:04:08.080
Assam can update whatever
their learnings are, Whatever

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:11.310
the information that they
want to share it with people.

00:04:11.311 --> 00:04:14.767
So it's the only audio-visual
interface where health workers

00:04:14.768 --> 00:04:17.590
would record an audio and
upload it over the system.

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:20.763
Uploading is not based on
their own network data, but

00:04:20.764 --> 00:04:25.500
network which is supported on
the health centers itself. Yeah.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.140
So currently,

00:04:26.141 --> 00:04:27.740
what we are,
what stage we are in,

00:04:27.741 --> 00:04:31.020
we have done some studies
with 60 health workers, so

00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:34.520
this is one snapshot of when
we were doing evaluation.

00:04:34.521 --> 00:04:37.211
So we have done studies with
some 60 health workers and

00:04:37.212 --> 00:04:38.708
the results are encouraging.

00:04:38.709 --> 00:04:40.935
So we are doing the next
study in January,

00:04:40.936 --> 00:04:43.163
which is with 500
health workers, and

00:04:43.164 --> 00:04:45.965
trying to see if we can
increase the learnability and

00:04:45.966 --> 00:04:49.381
memorability of the health
contents, Specifically in mental

00:04:49.382 --> 00:04:52.440
and child health and see if it
can create an impact of it.

00:04:52.441 --> 00:04:54.190
So this is the first project.

00:04:54.191 --> 00:04:56.689
We are still on the project,
we still have one more year,

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.198
one and
a half year on the project,

00:04:58.199 --> 00:04:59.880
then hoping to see
some good results.

00:04:59.881 --> 00:05:03.930
But the idea is that we deploy
the solution across this,

00:05:03.931 --> 00:05:07.290
which would have more than
50,000 health workers.

00:05:07.291 --> 00:05:11.332
Okay, the second one is the
earlier speaker had knowledge

00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:12.083
about TB.

00:05:12.084 --> 00:05:15.237
The second one is a project that
we are doing on called faster

00:05:15.238 --> 00:05:18.150
which is again complete
tuberculosis care we call it.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:22.240
So very quickly, the kind of
challenges that the TB ecosystem

00:05:22.241 --> 00:05:25.810
has, And in their first is the
poor referral system, that means

00:05:25.811 --> 00:05:29.420
if I'm a citizen and I may
be a prospective TB patient.

00:05:29.421 --> 00:05:32.900
There is a process that
a health worker refers to

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:36.380
the health system that I may
be a Tuberculosis patient.

00:05:36.381 --> 00:05:39.132
Second is tracking of initial
and retreatment defaulters.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:43.830
That means, if I am identified
as a TB patient, one option is

00:05:43.831 --> 00:05:46.010
that I don't even enroll
into the government schemes.

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.900
How do I track if I
don't enroll, and

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:50.320
eventually the person
would get into very

00:05:50.321 --> 00:05:51.820
serious stages of tuberculosis.

00:05:51.821 --> 00:05:56.580
Or I start consuming medicines,
but I don't complete the course.

00:05:56.581 --> 00:05:59.470
So then again, I go from
category one to category two or

00:05:59.471 --> 00:06:00.690
three patients.

00:06:00.691 --> 00:06:02.750
So then how do we track
these initial and

00:06:02.751 --> 00:06:04.360
retreatment defaulters?

00:06:04.361 --> 00:06:08.522
Third is the DOTS consumption,
how do we real-time track DOTS

00:06:08.523 --> 00:06:12.771
consumption, 99DOTS has been
doing amazing work onto that.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:15.683
And there are two major other
things which are a part of

00:06:15.684 --> 00:06:16.870
project test.

00:06:16.871 --> 00:06:19.140
All the health centers,
even public and private,

00:06:19.141 --> 00:06:20.710
they're completely disconnected.

00:06:20.711 --> 00:06:24.900
Specifically in Assam,
where most of the population, or

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:27.880
migrate from one place to
another place for work.

00:06:27.881 --> 00:06:30.375
So if the health centers
are not connected,

00:06:30.376 --> 00:06:33.815
the patient is enrolled into
the program from the starting of

00:06:33.816 --> 00:06:35.040
the program itself.

00:06:35.041 --> 00:06:38.132
So, and most often, they don't
even enroll into the program

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.754
because they have to,
they are daily wage workers.

00:06:40.755 --> 00:06:44.045
And second is, all these
problems lead basically to any

00:06:44.046 --> 00:06:47.415
kind of preventive measures,
which are often delayed.

00:06:47.416 --> 00:06:51.406
By the time the health
administrator would know that

00:06:51.407 --> 00:06:54.581
the patient is not
consuming medicines or

00:06:54.582 --> 00:06:59.491
not even registered into the
DOTS program, it's too delayed.

00:06:59.492 --> 00:07:00.785
And eventually,

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:04.770
all the government schemes
have become ineffective.

00:07:04.771 --> 00:07:07.117
So what we have
currently proposed,

00:07:07.118 --> 00:07:10.500
which we are currently in
the development stage, So

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:15.222
it's a complete ecosystem
which will connect patients,

00:07:15.223 --> 00:07:18.896
family members,
all the health providers,

00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:22.331
Which includes medical officers,
TB control units,

00:07:22.332 --> 00:07:25.766
STS Senior Technical
Supervisors, health workers,

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:29.425
DOT providers, all the officers
where the Top managing,

00:07:29.426 --> 00:07:32.630
the National Health Commission,
and so on.

00:07:32.631 --> 00:07:35.720
And also connect all
the private clinics and

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:39.450
the government clinics.

00:07:39.451 --> 00:07:41.965
So they somewhat
knew we are doing,

00:07:41.966 --> 00:07:44.627
just to give you a very quick
overviews, We are using this

00:07:44.628 --> 00:07:47.500
multi-technology platform
which includes them.

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:50.512
Mobile and IVR system based
on the technology literacy of

00:07:50.513 --> 00:07:53.461
the users, that means if
the health worker has specific

00:07:53.462 --> 00:07:54.716
technology literacy or

00:07:54.717 --> 00:07:58.036
the patient does not have at all
technology literacy, Then they

00:07:58.037 --> 00:08:00.779
can use different platform such
as IVR, giving a missed call or

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.620
just calling and entering
a particular number to it.

00:08:03.621 --> 00:08:06.832
So, and also we have introduced
one incentive-based system,

00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:08.852
which means it's not
a purely monitored

00:08:08.853 --> 00:08:10.284
incentive-based system.

00:08:10.285 --> 00:08:13.893
But the moment health workers
ensures that the patient is

00:08:13.894 --> 00:08:18.266
tracked, the health worker would
get 5 rupees of mobile recharge.

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:21.355
And similarly, every 15 days and
every one month,

00:08:21.356 --> 00:08:24.858
if the medicine consumption of
the patient is appropriate,

00:08:24.859 --> 00:08:28.590
as in regular, Then the patient
would again get some,

00:08:28.591 --> 00:08:32.170
every 15 days, they will get
5 rupees of mobile recharge.

00:08:32.171 --> 00:08:35.500
So that is, in a way,
they are trying to incentive and

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:37.128
see if that works out too,

00:08:37.129 --> 00:08:39.866
make sure that everyone
is on the platform.

00:08:39.867 --> 00:08:43.987
Very quickly, I'll touch, as in
how the whole ecosystem works if

00:08:43.988 --> 00:08:47.159
some patient is,
if he's a prospective patient.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.100
That means, he's coughing or has
some symptoms of tuberculosis,

00:08:50.101 --> 00:08:51.760
he's basically referred.

00:08:51.761 --> 00:08:54.632
He goes to the health center
where the health worker, or

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:56.831
we call it
an ANM Auxiliary Nurse Midwife,

00:08:56.832 --> 00:08:58.616
refers her on
the digital system.

00:08:58.617 --> 00:09:03.190
And then asks the patient to
visit the lab technician where

00:09:03.191 --> 00:09:07.295
the check-up will be done
to see whether a patient is

00:09:07.296 --> 00:09:11.697
a prospective patient,
converts into patient or not.

00:09:11.698 --> 00:09:15.282
So one of the major drawback
in the current TB ecosystem is

00:09:15.283 --> 00:09:19.019
there is no data that how many
prospective patient actually

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.827
converts into the patient.

00:09:20.828 --> 00:09:23.168
That's very critical because
they want to measure what

00:09:23.169 --> 00:09:25.706
location these people come from
and what are the age group and

00:09:25.707 --> 00:09:26.564
other parameters.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:29.158
That becomes very critical for
TB ecosystems, so

00:09:29.159 --> 00:09:31.260
that is one we are measuring.

00:09:31.261 --> 00:09:33.531
Second, once if
the patient is identified,

00:09:33.532 --> 00:09:36.460
as in the prospective patient
is identified as a patient,

00:09:36.461 --> 00:09:39.237
he's requested to enroll
into the DOT program again.

00:09:39.238 --> 00:09:42.105
Incentives comes over here the
moment the patient enrolls into

00:09:42.106 --> 00:09:44.930
the DOS program, to the patient
as well as the health worker.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:49.414
Then the medicine consumption
is typically dragged by the IVR

00:09:49.415 --> 00:09:52.240
system that we
are currently developing.

00:09:52.241 --> 00:09:56.981
And then all the patient family
members and medical officers and

00:09:56.982 --> 00:09:59.275
all the related stakeholder.

00:09:59.276 --> 00:10:02.343
So the TB ecosystem are there
into the loop knowing what

00:10:02.344 --> 00:10:06.160
the patient is doing exactly
at that point of the time.

00:10:06.161 --> 00:10:10.100
And yeah, and once the whole six
months patient system is over,

00:10:10.101 --> 00:10:13.870
then we hope that
the patient gets cured.

00:10:13.871 --> 00:10:17.745
So yeah, just completing.

00:10:17.746 --> 00:10:20.327
[LAUGH] I'm almost done, yeah.

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:23.722
So we are hoping that we'll
launch this in one district,

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:27.966
which is, it's a district of
3,000 tuberculosis patients, but

00:10:27.967 --> 00:10:30.527
hopefully, we
are starting with 500.

00:10:30.528 --> 00:10:32.757
The government wanted to
start with directly 3,000,

00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:34.750
which seems to be
a little bit impossible.

00:10:34.751 --> 00:10:38.070
But anyway, so
that's the current ecosystem.

00:10:38.071 --> 00:10:41.970
Just one last slide that we
are also sort of discussing with

00:10:41.971 --> 00:10:45.518
the USC on collaborating on
how we can predict, whether

00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:49.490
the prospective, other patient
would be followed or not.

00:10:49.491 --> 00:10:53.060
And how we can predict,
whether the health workers would

00:10:53.061 --> 00:10:56.780
be motivated enough to be
a part of the ecosystem,

00:10:56.781 --> 00:10:59.470
because motivation is
another major challenge.

00:10:59.471 --> 00:11:00.830
Thank you.

00:11:00.831 --> 00:11:02.582
I'm sorry, I took too
many of your questions.

00:11:02.583 --> 00:11:04.067
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Thank you sir.

